    <DataNode elementId="AT4G32810-MONOMER" textLabel="oxidoreductase, acting on single donors with incorporation of molecular oxygen, incorporation of two atoms of oxygen" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8VY26" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The |FRAME: AT4G32810 CCD8| gene is one of nine |FRAME: TAX-3702 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;| genes that encode carotenoid dioxygenases. The gene encodes a |FRAME: AT4G32810-MONOMER 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal cleavage dioxygenase|, an enzyme that catalyzes a complex oxigenation/rearrangement of |FRAME: CPD-14647 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal|, generating |FRAME: CPD-14649 carlactone|, an intermediate leading to production of strigolactones |CITS: [22422982]|. As typical to genes involved in this pathway, mutants in CCD8 display a dramatic increase in lateral branching |CITS: [ 12815068]|. In an earlier work the protein was co-expressed with |FRAME: AT2G44990 CCD7| in carotenoid-accumulating strains of &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;. It was found that the recombinant protein catalyzed the cleavage of |FRAME: CPD-13368 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal| (produced by CCD7) to |FRAME: CPD-13369 13-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenone| and a C9 dialdehyde |CITS: [15342640]|. However, later work has shown that the &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; substrate of the enzyme is |FRAME: CPD-14647 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal|, and that CCD8 alone is sufficient for conversion of this compound into a strigolactone-like compound |CITS: [22422982]|. It was also shown that the reaction with |FRAME: CPD-14647 9-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal| is 10-fold faster than that with |FRAME: CPD-13368 &lt;i&gt;all-trans&lt;/i&gt;-10&apos;-apo-&amp;beta;-carotenal| |CITS: [22422982]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G32810-MONOMER" />
